---
// Washington My Health My Data Act (RCW 19.373) consumer health data privacy policy. It must be
// linked from the homepage (the footer link counts). Reviewed by the practice before publishing.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import { practice } from '../data/practice';

const updated = 'November 18, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy | S+ Dental"
  fullTitle
  breadcrumb="Consumer health data privacy"
  description="How S+ Dental's website collects, uses, and shares consumer health data under Washington's My Health My Data Act, and how to exercise your rights."
>
  <PageBanner title="Consumer health data privacy" />

  <section class="band legal-text">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p><em>Last updated {updated}</em></p>

      <p>
        Washington's My Health My Data Act gives you rights over "consumer health data," which can
        include information that shows you may be looking for health care, such as visiting a
        dentist's website. This policy explains what the {practice.name} website collects and how
        you can control it. Your dental records and other information we keep as your health care
        provider are protected by HIPAA and described in our Notice of Privacy Practices, available
        at the office; this policy does not cover them.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Website analytics, only if you click Accept:</strong> pages you view on this site
          (for example, the services page), how you arrived, clicks on the appointment button, browser
          and device type, and approximate (city-level) location derived from your IP address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payments you choose to make:</strong> when you pay through a payment link we send,
          Stripe collects your card and contact details and gives us a record of the payment (amount,
          date, name, and email).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Messages you send us</strong> by email or phone.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We collect analytics directly from your browser through Google Analytics. Payment records
        come from Stripe. Appointment requests are collected by Calendly on its own site, under its
        own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Analytics: to understand how many people use the website and which pages help them.</li>
        <li>Payments and messages: to apply payments to your account and to reply to you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use this information for advertising, and we do not sell it.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share it only with service providers that process it for us: Google (Google Analytics
        and website hosting) and Stripe (payments). We do not share it with any other third parties
        or affiliates.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>confirm whether we collect, share, or sell your consumer health data, and get a copy;</li>
        <li>get a list of the third parties and affiliates we share it with;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time: use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of any page;</li>
        <li>ask us to delete your consumer health data.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Analytics data is not linked to your name, so we usually cannot find a single person's
        browsing history in it; clearing your cookies or withdrawing consent stops further
        collection, and Google deletes analytics data after the retention period set in our account.
      </p>
      <p>
        To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${practice.email}`}>{practice.email}</a> or call{' '}
        <a href={`tel:${practice.phone.tel}`}>{practice.phone.display}</a>. We will respond within
        45 days. If we decline your request, you can appeal by replying to our decision with
        "Appeal" in the subject; we will answer within 45 days, and if you are still not satisfied
        you may contact the Washington State Attorney General at
        <a href="https://www.atg.wa.gov/file-complaint" rel="noopener">atg.wa.gov/file-complaint</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-text .narrow {
    text-align: left;
  }
  .legal-text h2 {
    margin-top: 1.6em;
  }
  .legal-text ul {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .legal-text li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5em;
  }
</style>
